{"status":"completed","summary":"Configured node1 as a persistent, read-only TFTP server for the approved boot tree. Node2 downloads both approved files with matching hashes; uploads, overwrites, and traversal outside the boot root are rejected. Both nodes were restarted sequentially and fully recovered with changed boot identities.","actions_performed":["Installed the CentOS Stream 10 distribution-provided tftp-server package without changing the OS release or kernel.","Set /srv/legacy2/tftp-firmware-distribution/boot as the secure TFTP root.","Applied persistent SELinux labels, non-writable permissions, systemd read-only hardening, and a node2-scoped firewall rule.","Configured node2 connection tracking for TFTP data-channel replies.","Verified approved downloads, byte-preserving firmware transfer, upload rejection, overwrite rejection, and path-traversal rejection.","Restarted node1 and node2 individually and verified post-restart recovery."],"evidence":[{"requirement":"Publish only the approved boot tree as a read-only TFTP root","command_ids":["cmd-251f7606e4a54a6b","cmd-a22f6f9a6c64491f"],"summary":"Effective service configuration uses the boot directory as its secure root; permissions, SELinux labels, hardening, UDP/69 listener, and firewall scope are shown before and after restart."},{"requirement":"Node2 can download boot.cfg and firmware.bin with firmware bytes preserved","command_ids":["cmd-b797f136e95d459d","cmd-9641afcac1214edb"],"summary":"Both files downloaded successfully before and after restarts; SHA-256 hashes match the staged source hashes."},{"requirement":"Uploads, overwrites, and requests outside the boot root are rejected","command_ids":["cmd-f275761f62f34005","cmd-8b76d3ec11964e36","cmd-e19eba16792d49cd","cmd-fd1a695d7fc347f7"],"summary":"TFTP rejected new-file creation, approved-file overwrite, and ../private traversal. No unauthorized files appeared and approved source hashes remained unchanged."},{"requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software","command_ids":["cmd-82a04c19fed941c5","cmd-a67ce506185d43a6","cmd-fd1a695d7fc347f7"],"summary":"The distribution-provided tftp-server 5.2-51.el10 was installed; final state remains CentOS Stream 10 with kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node1 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-774c3ddaa2bb42c2","cmd-d1f85565205d4dbd","cmd-b089845483d24c18","cmd-a22f6f9a6c64491f","cmd-d28c603eff644f24"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 0581c914-b77e-45ce-b511-c0c9f578a303 to e8a10c02-4722-46ca-83a6-12b91191be20. The TFTP socket, security state, data hashes, and end-to-end downloads recovered."},{"requirement":"Mandatory node2 restart and recovery","command_ids":["cmd-64b453e2525b4683","cmd-0369fee1f7074379","cmd-89d8a3018f14484a","cmd-9641afcac1214edb","cmd-e19eba16792d49cd"],"summary":"Boot ID changed from 96974ac3-f19e-45f7-9672-e880dd505cf8 to 2787fc4b-d54f-4eed-b702-3df946b23e60. Firewalld and the TFTP helper recovered, approved downloads matched, and rejection controls remained effective."}]}
